ficial servers: before joining a ranked server, an official casual one with secure_connection_to_official_casual_servers, or one not yet on the server list, the client fetches a connect token from connect_token_provider (https://hypersomnia.io/connect_token) and connects with it, so the session keys are known only to it and that server; an official server starts netcode with the key derived from its official_server_secret and also takes insecure tokens, telling the connections apart by the server id in the token's user data; authentication only ever goes over a secure connection - clients send no tickets over insecure ones and servers ignore them, ranked servers kick insecure clients with the reason, a missing token where it is required stops the client before connecting - and the Steam ticket identity is the challenge plus the id of the official server the token was issued for, so a ticket given to one official server can not be passed on to another","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:44:00Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"687a89d7959ca071b0c3544f8eb8d5a4ec2b01c5","github_link":"https://github.com/TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia/commit/687a89d7959ca071b0c3544f8eb8d5a4ec2b01c5","commit_subject":"Masterserver: /connect_token?server=<ip:port or WebRTC id> issues a secure connect token for an official server - encrypted with that server's netcode key (derived from its official_server_secret), valid for 60 s, with \"HSEC1\" and the server id in the user data - and returns it with the client id and the server id as JSON; 404 for anything not currently listed as official, at most 30 requests a minute per IP (X-Real-IP when proxied from localhost); the targets are rebuilt on the main thread whenever the list, an official status or official_servers.d changes","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"sumatrapdfreader/sumatrapdf","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:43:57Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"ba5ff1df0e6bcbc37937c3